    "d2direct3d.dll_ConvertDDSurfaceRGB565ToRGB888": {
      "addresses": {
        "LoD/1.07": "0x6F8A3150"
      },
      "rvas": {
        "LoD/1.07": "0x3150"
      },
      "sizes": {
        "LoD/1.07": 1
      },
      "name": "ConvertDDSurfaceRGB565ToRGB888",
      "signature": "int ConvertDDSurfaceRGB565ToRGB888(byte * pbOutputBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Converts DirectDraw surface RGB565 pixel data to RGB888 format\n  \nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize array of 30 row pointers on stack (dwStack_7c=0x7c)\n  2. Check if global g_pDDSurfaceOld surface pointer is NULL, return 0 if null\n  3. Lock surface via vtable+0x64 (IDirectDrawSurface::Lock), fill row ptr array\n  4. If lock fails (iVar3!=0), call FUN_6f8a4120 error handler and return 0\n  5. Outer loop: iterate nIterCount from 0 to g_dwBinkHeightTable-1\n  6. Inner loop: iterate nColCount from 0 to g_dwBinkWidthTable-1\n     - Read 16-bit RGB565 wValue from current surface row pointer\n     - Extract R (bits 15-11, 5-bit) to byte 0: (wValue>>8)&0xf8\n     - Extract G (bits 10-5, 6-bit) to byte 1: ((wValue>>5)<<2)&0xff\n     - Extract B (bits 4-0, 5-bit) to byte 2: (wValue<<3)&0xff\n     - Write 3 bytes to pbDest output buffer, advance by 3 bytes\n  7. Unlock surface via vtable+0x80 (IDirectDrawSurface::Unlock)\n  8. Return 1 if unlock succeeds, else call FUN_6f8a4120 and return 0\n\nParameters:\n  ECX=pbOutputBuffer: Pointer to buffer for RGB888 output (3 bytes per pixel)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX=1: Both lock and unlock succeeded\n  EAX=0: Lock failed, unlock failed, or surface is NULL\n\nNotes:\n  RGB565 format: RRRRRGGGGGGBBBBB (bits 15-0)\n  RGB888 format: RRRRRRR0 GGGGGG00 BBBBB000 (per byte)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:1de091de38a0c8104999bec46fd52d0f",
      "instruction_counts": {
        "LoD/1.07": 1
      },
      "stack_frame_sizes": {
        "LoD/1.07": 132
      },
      "basic_block_counts": {
        "LoD/1.07": 1
      },
      "loop_counts": {
        "LoD/1.07": 0
      },
      "mnemonic_hashes": {
        "LoD/1.07": "1de091de38a0c8104999bec46fd52d0f"
      }
    },
