      "comment": "Array table lookup for element transformation values used during map initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load base address of transformation table (g_adElementTransformTable)\n2. Calculate offset: base + (dwElementIndex * 4) to get uint-sized entry\n3. Dereference pointer to retrieve transformed value\n4. Return transformed value\n\nParameters:\ndwElementIndex - Index into element transformation table (0-based offset into array)\n\nReturns:\nuint - Transformed element value from table, or undefined if index out of bounds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Used only for map versions < 7 during InitializeMapElementData\n- Table contains pre-calculated transformation values for map element processing\n- Index should be validated by caller; no bounds checking performed here\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x4 - Stride (size of uint, 4 bytes per table entry)\n0x6fde1c68 - Base address of g_adElementTransformTable\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeMapElementData - Calls this function to transform element values during version < 7 map loading",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d7897101f3cb99eb3b89274dfb087bc9",
