      "name": "InitializeGameState",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameState(dword * pGameState)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes the global game state buffer by copying from source to destination.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Save registers ESI and EDI\n  2. Load source pointer into ESI (ECX parameter)\n  3. Set copy count to 0x48 (72 DWORDs = 288 bytes)\n  4. Load destination address 0x6f8b9740 into EDI\n  5. Execute REP MOVSD (repeat move DWORD) to copy source to destination\n  6. Update global pointer g_pGameState to reference the copied buffer\n  7. Restore registers and return\n\nParameters:\n  pGameState (ECX): Pointer to source game state data (72 DWORDs)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Global g_aGameState is populated with copy of input data\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field | Type | Description\n  0      | 288  | data  | dword[72] | Game state array (72 DWORD elements)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:123e4e5d4b2315b8f7204bb9886e6a98",
