      "name": "ConvertPalettedToRGB16",
      "signature": "void ConvertPalettedToRGB16(byte * pbSrcPixels, ushort * pwDestPixels, int nWidth, int nHeight, int nDestPitch)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts 8-bit palette-indexed pixel data to 16-bit RGB565 color values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Validate height > 0, exit if no rows to process\n  2. For each row (nHeight iterations):\n     a. Initialize row pointers from current src/dest positions\n     b. For each pixel in row (nWidth iterations):\n        - Read 8-bit palette index from source\n        - Look up 16-bit RGB565 color from g_awPaletteColorLUT[index]\n        - Write 16-bit color to destination\n        - Advance both pointers by element size\n     c. Advance source by nWidth bytes (next row in source)\n     d. Advance dest by nDestPitch words (supports non-contiguous surfaces)\n  3. Return when all rows processed\n\nParameters:\n  pbSrcPixels (ECX) - Pointer to 8-bit palette-indexed source pixels\n  pwDestPixels (EDX) - Pointer to 16-bit RGB565 destination surface\n  nWidth - Width of tile in pixels (typically 0x20 = 32)\n  nHeight - Height of tile in pixels (typically 0x20 = 32)\n  nDestPitch - Destination surface pitch in 16-bit words (allows stride)\n\nReturns:\n  void - Writes converted pixels directly to destination buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - nHeight <= 0: Returns immediately without processing\n  - nWidth <= 0: Skips inner loop, advances to next row\n  - nDestPitch allows non-contiguous destination (pitch > width)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:37061fd055601bba6b2325740d4974b8",
