      "name": "CreateMemorySurfaceTexture",
      "signature": "int CreateMemorySurfaceTexture(void * * ppSurface, void * * ppTexture, dword dwHeight, dword dwWidth)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Creates a DirectDraw memory surface and obtains its IDirect3DTexture2 interface.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize DDSURFACEDESC structure (size 0x7c/124 bytes)\n  2. Zero out the structure fields (30 DWORDs via REP STOSD)\n  3. Set dwFlags to 0x1007 (DDSD_CAPS | DDSD_WIDTH | DDSD_HEIGHT | DDSD_PIXELFORMAT)\n  4. Copy pixel format from g_ddPixelFormat565 (RGB565 format, 32 bytes)\n  5. Set dwWidth and dwHeight from parameters\n  6. Set ddsCaps to 0x840 (DDSCAPS_TEXTURE | DDSCAPS_SYSTEMMEMORY)\n  7. Call IDirectDraw::CreateSurface via vtable offset 0x18\n  8. On success, query for IDirect3DTexture2 interface via QueryInterface\n  9. On texture query failure, release surface and return 0\n\nParameters:\n  ppSurface (ECX) - Output pointer to receive IDirectDrawSurface pointer\n  ppTexture (EDX) - Output pointer to receive IDirect3DTexture2 pointer\n  dwHeight (stack) - Surface height in pixels\n  dwWidth (stack) - Surface width in pixels\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Success, both surface and texture created\n  0 - Failure, CreateSurface failed or texture interface query failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Surface is released if texture query fails (cleanup on partial failure)\n  - Uses system memory for texture (DDSCAPS_SYSTEMMEMORY)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:a673b2a0c9c37613d3192693751c1d42",
