      "name": "CreateDeviceSurfaceTexture",
      "signature": "BOOL CreateDeviceSurfaceTexture(void * * ppSurface, void * * ppTexture, DWORD dwWidth, DWORD dwHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "BOOL",
      "comment": "Creates a DirectDraw surface and obtains an IDirect3DTexture2 interface for it.\\n\\n  Algorithm:\\n    1. Initialize DDSURFACEDESC2 structure (0x7C bytes) with zeros\\n    2. Set dwFlags to 0x1007 (DDSD_CAPS|DDSD_HEIGHT|DDSD_WIDTH|DDSD_PIXELFORMAT)\\n    3. Copy default pixel format from g_DefaultPixelFormat (32 bytes)\\n    4. Set surface dimensions from dwWidth and dwHeight parameters\\n    5. Configure surface caps based on g_bUseAgpMemory flag:\\n       - If AGP: 0x00005000 (DDSCAPS_TEXTURE|DDSCAPS_VIDEOMEMORY)\\n       - If VRAM: 0x10005000 (DDSCAPS_TEXTURE|DDSCAPS_VIDEOMEMORY|DDSCAPS_NONLOCALVIDMEM)\\n    6. Call IDirectDraw7::CreateSurface (vtable offset 0x18)\\n    7. On success, QueryInterface for IID_IDirect3DTexture2\\n    8. If QueryInterface fails, release surface and return 0\\n\\n  Parameters:\\n    ppSurface (ECX)  - Output pointer to receive IDirectDrawSurface7 interface\\n    ppTexture (EDX)  - Output pointer to receive IDirect3DTexture2 interface  \\n    dwWidth          - Surface width in pixels\\n    dwHeight         - Surface height in pixels\\n\\n  Returns:\\n    1 (TRUE)  - Surface and texture created successfully\\n    0 (FALSE) - Creation failed (DDERR_UNSUPPORTED silently ignored)\\n\\n  Special Cases:\\n    - DDERR_UNSUPPORTED (0x8876017c) is silently ignored (returns 0 without logging)\\n    - Other DirectDraw errors are logged via FUN_6f8a4120\\n    - Direct3D errors are logged via FUN_6f8a3b00\\n    - Surface is released if texture interface query fails",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:0b18abb02356d9a4763cff9aba088d71",
