      "name": "ClearRenderSurface",
      "signature": "void ClearRenderSurface(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Clears the render surface by locking and zeroing all pixels.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Select surface pointer: g_pClipper if available, else g_pBackSurfaceCOM\n  2. Initialize array of 30 surface line pointers (apSurfaceLines)\n  3. Call surface Lock method (offset 0x64) with flags 0x21 to lock surface\n  4. If lock failed: Log error via FUN_6f8a4120 and return\n  5. If lock succeeded: For each of g_dwBinkHeightTable rows:\n     - Clear dwSurfaceStride bytes via apSurfaceLines[3] using STOSD/STOSB\n     - Advance line pointer by dwSurfaceStride bytes\n  6. Call surface Unlock method (offset 0x80) to unlock and present changes\n  7. Return\n\nParameters:\n  (none - uses global g_pClipper, g_pBackSurfaceCOM, g_dwBinkHeightTable)\n\nReturns:\n  void (always succeeds after returning from function; errors handled internally)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Falls back to g_pBackSurfaceCOM if g_pClipper is NULL\n  - Handles both 32-bit (DWORD) and 8-bit (BYTE) writes depending on alignment\n  - Lock failure is logged but function still returns normally",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:ab59b566f84a5721491fde7a2a4ac810",
