      "name": "HandleDirect3DError",
      "signature": "void HandleDirect3DError(uint dwDevice, int nErrorCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Handles Direct3D error codes by logging appropriate error messages and dispatching to error processing function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if error code is positive or zero (success/standard case)\n  2. If positive, dispatch to FUN_6f8a4120 for processing\n  3. If zero, log generic Direct3D error and return\n  4. If negative, normalize error code (add 0x7789fd44) to get table index\n  5. Verify index is within bounds (0x0 to 0x4b / 75 decimal)\n  6. If in bounds, use jump table to load appropriate error message string\n  7. Log the error message with QueueLogMessage and return\n  8. If out of bounds, dispatch to FUN_6f8a4120 for special handling\n\nParameters:\n  dwDevice (ECX): Device handle or identifier\n  nErrorCode (EDX): Direct3D error code to handle\n\nReturns:\n  None (void). All error handling done via side effects: QueueLogMessage or dispatch to FUN_6f8a4120\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Zero error code: logs generic error message\n  - Negative error codes: normalized via offset 0x7789fd44 for jump table indexing\n  - Out-of-range errors: dispatched to FUN_6f8a4120 for extended processing\n  - Positive errors: immediately dispatched to FUN_6f8a4120",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
