      "name": "InitializeFontTextures",
      "signature": "int * InitializeFontTextures(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Initializes font rendering textures and font rasterization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Create display device context (DC) via CreateDCA\n  2. Create 10pt Courier font via CreateFontA (0xA)\n  3. Create 8x16 device-independent bitmap (DIB) via CreateBitmap\n  4. Select font and bitmap into DC\n  5. Set text color to DAT_6f8b4d88 (foreground), background to DAT_6f8bacb0\n  6. Create 8x16 pixel in-memory surface via CreateMemorySurfaceTexture\n  7. Loop through ASCII characters 0x20 (32 space) to 0x7F (127 DEL):\n     a. Render character glyph to bitmap via DrawTextA\n     b. Lock memory surface via Lock vtable call [offset 0x64]\n     c. Read pixel data from DC via GetPixel for each 8x16 pixel\n     d. Write 0xFFFF (opaque) for foreground pixels, 0x0000 for background\n     e. Unlock memory surface via Unlock vtable call [offset 0x80]\n     f. Create device surface texture from memory surface\n     g. If transparency mask set: copy surface data, else copy texture data\n  8. After loop, initialize global transform/projection matrices\n  9. Get character widths 0x20-0x7F via GetCharWidthA into g_dwCharWidths\n\nParameters:\n  (None - uses global device/texture state)\n\nReturns:\n  Pointer to initialized font data buffer (success)\n  Calls FUN_6f8aaff9(-1) on failure (assertion exit)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Creates 256 character glyphs (0x20 to 0x7E + overflow handling)\n  - Handles transparency mask via g_dwTransparencyMask check\n  - Initializes 31 float-format matrix elements for 3D rendering",
