      "name": "RemoveListNode",
      "signature": "void RemoveListNode(int nListControl, int nIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Removes a node from a doubly-linked list by index\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Verify list is not empty (pListControl + 0x4 != 0)\n  2. Get first node from list (pListControl + 0x8)\n  3. Calculate target node address: pListControl[0x18] + nIndex * 0x18\n  4. If target is first node, update first pointer (pListControl + 0x8)\n  5. If target is not last node, handle middle removal by updating pointers\n  6. Move node to free list at pListControl + 0x10\n  7. Decrement item count (pListControl + 0x4)\n\nParameters:\n  ECX pListControl - Pointer to list control structure\n  EDX nIndex - Index of node to remove\n    \nReturns:\n  void (modifies list in-place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty list: Returns immediately without changes\n  - Single node: Clears free list pointers\n  - First node: Updates list head pointer\n  - Last node: Updates list tail pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
