      "name": "InitPerspectiveLookupTable",
      "signature": "void InitPerspectiveLookupTable(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes the perspective distance lookup table for 3D coordinate transformations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Iterates from index -0x1000 (-4096) to 0xFFF (4095), total 0x2000 (8192) entries\n  2. Clamps each index to range [-2999, 2999] (0xBB6/0xBB7 boundaries)\n  3. Computes perspective value: 0x2EE000 (3,072,000) / (clampedIndex - 3000)\n  4. Stores result in g_aPerspectiveLUT at corresponding position\n  5. Sets g_dwZoomScale to 0x100 (256) as default zoom factor\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Index < -0xBB6 (-2998): Uses -2999 for calculation (divisor = -5999)\n  - Index > 0xBB6 (2998): Uses 2999 for calculation (divisor = -1)\n  - Middle range: Uses actual index (divisor ranges from -5998 to -2)\n  - Division by zero avoided: minimum divisor magnitude is 1 (at index 2999)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  - 0x1000 (4096): Half the table size, starting offset\n  - 0x2000 (8192): Total table entries / loop termination\n  - 0xBB6/0xBB7 (2998/2999): Clamping boundaries\n  - 0x2EE000 (3,072,000): Perspective scaling constant\n  - 0x100 (256): Default zoom scale (8.8 fixed-point 1.0)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:3b4952349ed945130b7594063d40c9ef",
