      "name": "TransformWorldToScreen",
      "signature": "void TransformWorldToScreen(int nWorldX, int nWorldY, int nZoom, int * pScreenX, int * pScreenY)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Transforms world coordinates to screen coordinates using perspective projection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Compute relative offsets from perspective anchor point (g_dwPerspectiveOffsetX, Y)\n  2. Calculate intermediate coordinate sum (nXPlusDeltaX)\n  3. Compute scaled zoom factor from perspective LUT indexed by (param_3, nXPlusDeltaX)\n  4. Apply perspective scaling to compute screen X coordinate\n  5. Apply perspective scaling to compute screen Y coordinate (-0x20 offset, center on render height/2)\n  6. Output screen coordinates to param_4 (pScreenX), param_5 (pScreenY)\n\nParameters:\n  nWorldX (ECX)   World space X coordinate\n  nWorldY (EDX)   World space Y coordinate\n  nZoom           Zoom/distance factor (indexes perspective LUT)\n  pScreenX        Pointer to output screen X coordinate\n  pScreenY        Pointer to output screen Y coordinate\n\nReturns:\n  void (output via pScreenX, pScreenY pointers)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses 0x1000 subtraction to ensure positive LUT index\n  - Applies 0x1fff mask to LUT index (8191 elements)\n  - Centers X on g_nBinkRenderWidth / 2\n  - Centers Y on g_nBinkRenderHeight / 2 with -0x20 offset\n  - Fixed-point arithmetic with 0x10 (16) and 0x14 (20) bit shifts for precision\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset|Size|Field|Type|Description\n  0x0   |4   |g_dwPerspectiveOffsetX|dword|World space X reference point\n  0x4   |4   |g_dwPerspectiveOffsetY|dword|World space Y reference point\n  0x0   |?   |g_aPerspectiveLUT|dword[]|Perspective scale lookup table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CON",
      "index": "CON:96ac9a5d9977afc69dbb2188614dba72",
