      "name": "FreeDirectoryData",
      "signature": "void FreeDirectoryData(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Releases and clears the global directory data allocation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check if g_pDirectoryData is allocated (non-zero)\n  2. If allocated, call ReleasePoolAllocation with pool ID 0x59 (89)\n  3. Clear the global pointer to zero after release\n  4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  None - function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\n  void - no return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_pDirectoryData is NULL/zero, release is skipped\n  - Always clears global pointer regardless of release result",
