      "name": "InitializeDirectoryData",
      "signature": "void InitializeDirectoryData(uint dwFileType, uint dwReserved1, uint dwReserved2, uint dwReserved3)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes directory data buffer and optionally loads palette or smack video data.\n  \n  Algorithm:\n  1. Pre-initialization: Call FUN_6f8ab210()\n  2. Check shutdown flag (g_bGameShutdown)\n  3. Validate g_pDirectoryData pointer (assert if null)\n  4. Zero-initialize g_pDirectoryData buffer (0x4000 DWORDs)\n  5. Post-initialization: Call FUN_6f8a73f0()\n  6. Handle surface operations based on transparency mask\n  7. Load palette or video data if requested via stack parameter\n  \n  Parameters:\n    dwFileType (uint, EAX): Type identifier for directory data operation\n    dwReserved1 (undefined4, EDX): Reserved/unused\n    dwReserved2 (undefined4, [ESP+8]): Reserved/unused\n    dwReserved3 (undefined4, [ESP+12]): Reserved/unused\n  \n  Returns:\n    void\n  \n  Special Cases:\n    - If g_bGameShutdown is set, skips buffer initialization\n    - If g_pDirectoryData is null, triggers FogAssert failure\n    - File loading ('p'/'s' parameter) handled via stack parameter at offset 0x71c8",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:546c17e22a38a8e15c8829671ea3e893",
