      "name": "InitializeSurfaceDimensions",
      "signature": "void InitializeSurfaceDimensions(int nSurface)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes surface dimension and scaling parameters\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load width and height from structure (offsets 0x4, 0x8)\n  2. Determine max dimension size based on thresholds:\n     - If both < 0x20 (32): set to 0x20\n     - Else if both < 0x80 (128): set to 0x80\n     - Else if both < 0x100 (256): set to 0x100\n  3. Store max dimensions at offsets 0x14, 0x18\n  4. Initialize scale factors to 1.0 (0x3f800000) at offsets 0x24, 0x2c\n  5. Initialize offset values to 0.0 at offsets 0x20, 0x28\n  6. Calculate area (width * height) and store at offset 0x1c\n\nParameters:\n  nSurface (ECX): Pointer to surface/dimension structure (passed as int)\n    Offset 0x4: width (dword)\n    Offset 0x8: height (dword)\n    Offset 0x14: max width (written)\n    Offset 0x18: max height (written)\n    Offset 0x1c: area (written as width*height)\n    Offset 0x20: offset x (written as 0.0)\n    Offset 0x24: scale x (written as 1.0)\n    Offset 0x28: offset y (written as 0.0)\n    Offset 0x2c: scale y (written as 1.0)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Dimension sizes are constrained to one of three power-of-2 values\n  - Scale factors are initialized to identity (1.0)\n  - Area is computed as product of constrained width and height",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
