      "name": "RenderSkillGlyphWithQuality",
      "signature": "void RenderSkillGlyphWithQuality(CelFileInfo * pCelInfo, int nParam2)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Render skill glyph with high rendering quality mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Set rendering quality to mode 0x4 (High Quality)\n  2. Load/retrieve cel frame data from provided CelFileInfo pointer\n  3. If load fails, assert with fatal error; if assertion error, abort execution\n  4. Extract CEL file metadata: table index, height, mode, DWORD field value\n  5. Adjust CEL mode and table index by adding 0x2 (offset adjustment)\n  6. Initialize render surface dimensions from adjusted parameters\n  7. Render skill glyph with 0x3 parameter\n  8. If rendering succeeds, set up Bink render quad with adjusted coordinates\n\nParameters:\n  pCelInfo   [ECX]  Pointer to CelFileInfo structure containing CEL file data\n  nParam2    [EDX]  Parameter used for coordinate adjustment (reduced by 1)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  CEL load failure: Asserts with fatal error (0xd0) if CelFileInfo is NULL\n  Rendering failure: If RenderSkillGlyph returns 0, skips Bink quad setup",
