      "name": "RemoveLinkedListNode",
      "signature": "void RemoveLinkedListNode(int * pList, int nItemIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Removes a node from a doubly-linked list cache structure by index.\n\nAlgorithm\n  1. Validate preconditions: list has elements, index is valid (0 < index <= max)\n  2. Calculate node address: list[6] (head pointer) + (index * 0x18) - 0x18\n  3. If node is head/tail, unlink from list endpoints\n  4. If node is middle, update neighbor links to bypass removed node\n  5. If list becomes empty, reset head and tail pointers\n  6. Link removed node to end of list for reuse/recycling\n\nParameters\n  pList: Pointer to list control structure (offsets: [0]=maxCount, [1]=itemCount, [2]=head, [3]=tail, [6]=nodeArray)\n  nItemIndex: 1-based index of item to remove from list\n\nReturns\n  void - modifies list structure in-place\n\nSpecial Cases\n  - If list.itemCount <= 1, function returns without modification\n  - Handles removal of head node (when index results in head pointer)\n  - Handles removal of tail node (when index results in tail pointer)\n  - Handles removal of middle node with proper link updates",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:052a101a230c3ddc22bbf8ff66201a19",
