      "name": "InitializeTextureCacheSlots",
      "signature": "int InitializeTextureCacheSlots(int * pCache, int nStartOffset, int nEndOffset, int nWidth, int nHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes a range of texture cache slots and allocates memory for surfaces.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Calculate total bytes needed: (nEndOffset - nStartOffset) / (g_dwBytesPerPixel * nWidth * nHeight)\n  2. Cap slot count at maximum 0x400 (1024)\n  3. Allocate memory for slot descriptors (32 bytes per slot)\n  4. Initialize allocated memory to zero using REP STOSD/STOSB\n  5. For each slot, create surface/texture pair via CreateDeviceSurfaceTexture\n  6. Link slots in doubly-linked list (field +0x18 and +0x1c)\n  7. Set cache pointers to first and last slots\n  8. Return total bytes successfully cached\n\nParameters:\n  pCache [ECX]     - Pointer to TextureCache structure (size 28 bytes)\n  nStartOffset [EDX] - Starting offset in source buffer\n  nEndOffset [Stack+4] - Ending offset in source buffer\n  nWidth [Stack+8] - Width of each texture\n  nHeight [Stack+12] - Height of each texture\n\nReturns:\n  Success (EAX) - Total bytes in cache (nSlots * bytes_per_slot + nStartOffset)\n  Partial (EAX) - Fewer slots on surface allocation failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If surface allocation fails, remaining uninitialized slots are skipped\n  - First slot linking sets +0x18 only (no previous)\n  - Last slot linking sets +0x1c only (no next)\n  - Middle slots link both directions",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:34e3fc1c63bfbcec77f205a7d9c64724",
