      "name": "CleanupRendererInventory",
      "signature": "void CleanupRendererInventory(int * pInventory, int nReleasePool)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Cleans up renderer inventory and releases allocated resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Validate pInventory is not NULL (assert at offset 0x71)\n  2. Check pInventory[6] (pool pointer); if NULL, validate pInventory[1] empty (assert at 0x74)\n  3. If pInventory[6] exists, iterate through max items (*pInventory):\n    - Call virtual destructor (vtable+0x8) for pInventory[6][i].field_0x14\n    - Call virtual destructor (vtable+0x8) for pInventory[6][i].field_0x10\n    - Each item occupies 0x20 (32) bytes\n  4. If bReleasePool != 0, process linked list of items:\n    - Unlink items from pInventory[1..3] (head/tail pointers)\n    - Clear item references in parent structure\n    - Link to free list at pInventory[4..5]\n  5. Call ReleasePoolAllocation() if pInventory[6] exists\n  6. Clear first 7 DWORDs of pInventory structure\n\nParameters:\n  pInventory (ECX): Pointer to inventory structure; offsets 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 18h used\n  bReleasePool (EDX): If non-zero, process and free inventory items; if 0, skip item cleanup\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Asserts if pInventory is NULL (calls FUN_6f8aaff9 with 0xFFFFFFFF)\n  - Asserts if pInventory[6] is NULL but pInventory[1] is non-zero\n  - Requires virtual destructor at offset +0x8 in referenced objects\n  - Memory model: Linked list for active items, free pool for released items",
