      "name": "MoveCacheItemToEnd",
      "signature": "void * MoveCacheItemToEnd(int * pCache, int nIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Moves a cache item to the end of the doubly-linked list (MRU pattern).\n\n  Algorithm:\n  1. Check if cache has more than 1 item (pCache[1] > 1)\n  2. Validate index: nIndex != 0 (INVALID_HARDWARE_ADDRESS), \n     nIndex <= pCache->nMaxNumItems, nIndex >= 1\n  3. Get head of linked list (pCache[2])\n  4. Calculate item address: pCache[6] + (nIndex * 0x20) - 0x20\n     where 0x20 (32) is the cache item size\n  5. Remove item from current position in doubly-linked list:\n     - If item is head: advance head to item->pNext\n     - If item is tail: advance tail to item->pPrev\n     - Otherwise: unlink from both neighbors\n  6. Clear item's prev/next pointers (offset 0x18/0x1c)\n  7. Append item to end of list (tail)\n\n  Parameters:\n    pCache (ECX) - Pointer to cache structure:\n      [0x00] nMaxNumItems - Maximum number of items\n      [0x04] nNumItems - Current item count  \n      [0x08] pHead - Head of linked list\n      [0x0C] pTail - Tail of linked list\n      [0x18] pItemArray - Base address of item array\n    nIndex (EDX) - 1-based index of item to move\n\n  Returns:\n    Pointer to the moved cache item, or NULL if cache is empty/invalid\n\n  Structure Layout (Cache Item at offsets 0x18/0x1c):\n    Offset | Size | Field    | Description\n    0x18   | 4    | pNext    | Next item in linked list\n    0x1C   | 4    | pPrev    | Previous item in linked list",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:052a101a230c3ddc22bbf8ff66201a19",
