      "name": "RenderTileWithBlending",
      "signature": "int RenderTileWithBlending(int * pTileMap, int nOffsetX, int nOffsetY, byte byBlendFactor, byte byAlpha, int nInitValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Renders a single tile with decompressed data and palette blending.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize viewport bounds via FUN_6f8aa030 (sets nMinX, nMinY, nMaxX, nMaxY)\n  2. Check if tile map has any tiles (count at offset 0x50)\n  3. Iterate through each tile entry in the tile array (offset 0x54, 0x14 bytes per entry)\n  4. Extract tile X,Y from tile data and add offset parameters\n  5. Validate coordinates are within viewport bounds\n  6. If valid: decompress tile data and setup vertex coordinates\n  7. Blend palette and render 0x1c4 (452) pixels via D3D device call\n  8. Return 1 if any tile rendered, 0 if none\n\nParameters:\n  pTileMap (ECX) - Pointer to tile map structure\n  nOffsetX (EDX) - X coordinate offset to add to tile positions\n  nOffsetY (Stack+0x4) - Y coordinate offset to add to tile positions  \n  byBlendFactor (Stack+0x8) - Blend/transparency factor (0-255)\n  byAlpha (Stack+0xc) - Alpha blending parameter\n  nInitValue (Stack+0x10) - Initialization value for FUN_6f8aa030\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 1 if any tile was rendered, 0 if no tiles in map or none in bounds",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:37f81d6b6408de2347833653b06bd947",
