      "name": "RenderTileData",
      "signature": "int RenderTileData(int nWorld, int nTileX, int nTileY, byte bColorR, byte bColorGBA, int nD3DDevice)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Renders isometric tile data to screen using Direct3D device.\n  \n  Algorithm:\n  1. Validate tile count at pWorld+0x50; return 0 if count < 1\n  2. Call FUN_6f8aa030(pD3DDevice, 1, &nViewMinY, &nOffset) for viewport setup\n  3. Load viewport bounds from stack variables (nViewMinY, nViewMaxX, nViewMaxY)\n  4. Shift tile coordinates: nTileXShifted = nTileX << 0xd (multiply by 8192)\n  5. Iterate through all tile rows (0 to tile count - 1)\n  6. Read tile metadata from pWorld+0x54[nTileIndex] (16-bit signed values)\n  7. Calculate grid coordinates: nTileRow>>5, nTileCol>>5 (divide by 32)\n  8. Transform 4 tile corners to screen space:\n     - Corner1: (nTileXShifted+0x18000, nTileYShifted+0x18000)\n     - Corner2: (nTileXShifted+0x38000, nTileYShifted+0x20000)\n     - Corner3: (nTileXShifted+0x28000, nTileYShifted+0x30000)\n     - Corner4: (nTileXShifted+0x08000, nTileYShifted+0x10000)\n  9. Store transformed screen coords in globals (g_fRenderCorner1X, etc)\n  10. Test visibility: any corner within viewport bounds [nViewMinY, nViewMaxX) x [nViewMinX, nViewMaxY)\n  11. If visible: call DecompressTileData to decompress LZSS data\n  12. Render 4x4 sub-tile grid via nested loop:\n      - For each 4x4 vertex: TransformWorldToScreen, SetPaletteBlendedColor\n      - Push colors and coordinates to buffer\n  13. Submit render buffer to D3D: g_pD3DDevice->DrawPrimitive(5, 0x1c4, buffer)\n  14. Return 1 if rendered, 0 if tile outside viewport\n  \n  Parameters:\n  pWorld (ECX)           World data structure (tile array at +0x54, count at +0x50)\n  nTileX (EDX)           Tile grid X coordinate (shifted by 0xd in algorithm)\n  nTileY (Stack+0x4)     Tile grid Y coordinate (shifted by 0xd in algorithm)\n  bColorR (Stack+0x8)    Red color channel (0x00-0xFF)\n  bColorGBA (Stack+0xC)  Green/Blue/Alpha packed value\n  pD3DDevice (Stack+0x10) Direct3D IUnknown device pointer\n  \n  Returns:\n  EAX = 1:  Tile visible and rendered to screen\n  EAX = 0:  Tile outside viewport bounds OR no tiles in world\n  \n  Special Cases:\n  - Early exit if tile count < 1 (return 0)\n  - Visibility check uses open bounds (strict < on max coordinates)\n  - Tile corners offset by 0x8000 (32768) for 4x4 sub-tile grid\n  - FPU registers used for floating-point coordinate transformation\n  - Global render buffers (g_fRenderCorner*) shared with TransformWorldToScreen",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
