      "name": "AdjustFileBufferBounds",
      "signature": "int AdjustFileBufferBounds(int nHeapState, int * pChunkHeader, byte * pbBlock, uint dwNewSizeUnits)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Resize a small block within a chunk-based memory allocator in place.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Read current block size from first byte of pbBlock (in 16-byte units)\n    2. Calculate chunk entry pointer from heap state array at offset 0x18\n       using page-aligned index: (pChunkHeader - heapBase) >> 0xc (12-bit shift = 4KB pages)\n    3. If shrinking (dwNewSizeUnits < dwOldSizeUnits):\n       - Update block size byte to new size\n       - Add freed units back to chunk entry free count\n       - Mark chunk entry with 0xf1 (dirty/modified flag)\n    4. If same size: Return 0 (no change needed)\n    5. If growing (dwNewSizeUnits > dwOldSizeUnits):\n       - Check if new end exceeds chunk boundary (pChunkHeader + 0x3e = 0xF8 bytes max)\n       - Scan bytes from old end to new end, verify all are 0x00 (free space)\n       - If any non-zero byte found, return 0 (cannot grow in place)\n       - Update block size byte\n       - If free pointer falls within expanded region, advance it past new end\n       - Count consecutive zero bytes after new end for free count\n       - Subtract expanded units from chunk entry free count\n\n  Parameters:\n    nHeapState      - Heap context with base address at +0x10 and chunk entries at +0x18\n    pChunkHeader    - Pointer to chunk header: [0]=free ptr, [4]=free count, [8]=data start\n    pbBlock         - Pointer to block data, first byte is size in 16-byte units\n    dwNewSizeUnits  - Requested new size in 16-byte units (0x10 bytes per unit)\n\n  Returns:\n    1 = Success (block resized in place)\n    0 = Failure (cannot resize: same size, boundary exceeded, or non-free bytes in path)\n\n  Structure Layout (Chunk Header at pChunkHeader):\n    Offset  Size  Field        Type     Description\n    0x00    4     pFreePtr     byte*    Pointer to next free space in chunk\n    0x04    4     nFreeCount   int      Count of consecutive free bytes at pFreePtr\n    0x08    0xF0  aBlockData   byte[]   Block data area (max 0xF8 total = pChunkHeader + 0x3e * 4)\n\n  Special Cases:\n    - 0xF1 flag at pnChunkEntry[1] indicates chunk was shrunk (dirty flag)\n    - Block size stored in first byte limits blocks to 255 * 16 = 4080 bytes max\n    - Chunk boundary check uses 0x3e offset (62 * 4 = 248 bytes = 0xF8 from header)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:83295157daa32d8a2ec17bdc4754c492",
