      "name": "InitializeCodePageLocale",
      "signature": "dword InitializeCodePageLocale(int nCodePage)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Initialize character type lookup table for code page\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Acquire CRT lock (0x19) for thread-safe access\n  2. Get current code page via FUN_6f8af382\n  3. Compare with cached g_dwCurrentCodePage\n  4. If match, return success (0)\n  5. If new code page:\n     a) Search pre-calculated tables in g_aCodePageTable\n     b) If found, use cached data\n     c) If not found, call GetCPInfo for OS code page info\n     d) Clear g_abyCharTypeTable (0x40 DWORDs)\n     e) Process lead byte ranges from CPINFO\n     f) Mark DBCS lead bytes (flag 0x4)\n     g) Mark trail byte ranges (flag 0x8)\n  6. Update cached values\n  7. Release CRT lock (0x19)\n\nParameters:\n  nCodePage - Code page ID (e.g., 932=Shift-JIS, 949=Korean)\n\nReturns:\n  0 (success) - Character types initialized\n  -1 (0xffffffff) - Failure, GetCPInfo failed",
